# ImplementationPattern: list of values of the GovernanceRules accelerator. How a data product designer implements a governance rule in a Semarchy data product.
_package: GovernanceRules.list_of_values
_type: LOVType
_name: ImplementationPattern
label: Implementation pattern
description: 'How a data product designer implements a governance rule in a Semarchy data product.'
length: 32
lovValues:
- code: VALIDATION
  label: Validation
  description: 'Implement the rule as a validation (SemQL, plugin, mandatory, list of values or unique key).'
- code: ENRICHER
  label: Enricher
  description: 'Implement the rule as an enricher that computes, normalizes or standardizes values.'
- code: PRIVILEGE_ROW_FILTER
  label: Privilege or row filter
  description: 'Implement the rule with privilege grants: entity and attribute access, row filters.'
- code: MATCHING_SURVIVORSHIP
  label: Matching and survivorship
  description: 'Implement the rule in match rules, merge thresholds or survivorship rules.'
- code: WORKFLOW
  label: Workflow
  description: 'Implement the rule as a workflow, for example an approval before a change is certified.'
- code: RETENTION_POLICY
  label: Retention policy
  description: 'Implement the rule with a data retention policy or historization settings.'
- code: DESCRIPTION_AI_INSTRUCTION
  label: Description and AI instruction
  description: 'Implement the rule in the descriptions of the model, including the AI agent instructions.'
- code: NAMING_CONVENTION
  label: Naming convention
  description: 'Implement the rule by following a naming convention for objects, attributes or codes.'
- code: REFERENCE_ENTITY
  label: Reference entity
  description: 'Implement the rule with a managed reference entity or a list of values instead of free text.'
